  "rationale": "The only closely matching evidence-supported optimization is dependency caching (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE), but it is contraindicated for this workflow. This is a PyPI publishing workflow that explicitly disables the uv cache with a documented security rationale: a poisoned cache entry could reach artifacts uploaded to PyPI. The pattern's own contraindications include mutable or untrusted cached content, which applies to a publishing job whose outputs are released to a public package index. The repository does have pyproject.toml and uv.lock, which would satisfy the cache key precondition, but the security boundary of the release job outweighs the modest measured benefit. No other pattern applies: there is no matrix (so fail-fast and cancel-stale are not relevant), the job already has an explicit timeout-minutes: 20, and this is a tag-triggered release workflow rather than a repeated branch/PR workflow where skipping or change filtering would be appropriate. Applying a cache here would weaken the intended supply-chain safety of the publishing job, so no change is supported.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
}
